# CLAUDE.md

This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.

## What this project is

A **Drupal 11 contribution workbench** — a local environment for contributing patches and MRs to Drupal.org contrib modules. There is no custom application code. All work targets modules under `{{DRUPAL_WEBROOT}}/modules/contrib/`.

The entry point for any contribution task is **`/drupal-issue-start <url>`** — give it an issue URL and it loads prior context, fetches live state, and waits for direction. From there it delegates to `drupal-issue-agent` for review and implementation work, or `drupal-issue-catchup` to sync after time away.

---

## Global Rule — Report Before Acting

Before any code change, file edit, git operation, or other write action: **present a structured findings report** describing what you found and what you plan to do, then wait for explicit approval. Reading, fetching, and analysis are always permitted without asking. A prior "go ahead" in the conversation does not carry forward — each new action phase requires fresh approval.

